          "english": "It's no secret in the advanced-math community that diversity is a problem. According to Mark Saul, the director of competitions for the Mathematical Association of America, not a single African-American or Hispanic student—and only a handful of girls—has ever made it to the Math Olympiad team in its 50 years of existence. Many schools simply don't prioritize academic competitions. \"Do you know who we have to beat?\" asked Saul. \"The football team, the basketball team—that's our competition for resources, student time, attention, school dollars, parent efforts, school enthusiasm.\"",
